## Security before deployment

The chat route declares FUNCTION authentication. Local Core Tools does not enforce
keys; in Azure send a key using `x-functions-key`. A key is application access control,
not per-user identity/authorization. Application logs contain sizes, not prompts or
completions; separately review provider SDK debug tracing and exception handling.
Configure gateway rate limits, concurrency/token limits, per-user quotas, provider
budgets and cost alerts before exposing a billable backend. Existing generated
projects are not rewritten by this template update.

